  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "OpenccNetLib v1.5.1\n\n            - Updated bundled dictionary data.\n            - Added flexible custom dictionary loading and post-load customization APIs for advanced OpenCC workflows.\n            - Added strongly typed `DictSlot`, `CustomDictSpec`, and `CustomDictMode` APIs for safe custom dictionary management.\n            - Added append and override modes for layering or replacing individual OpenCC dictionary slots.\n            - Added support for applying custom dictionaries from both external files and in-memory key/value pairs.\n            - Added support for sequential custom dictionary layering with deterministic precedence and metadata rebuilding.\n            - Added support for customizing dictionaries loaded from built-in, Zstd, CBOR, JSON, and pure file-based sources.\n            - Improved custom dictionary validation and slot safety to preserve OpenCC dictionary structure compatibility.\n            - Improved dictionary serialization APIs to support serializing already customized `DictionaryMaxlength` instances.\n            - Refactored `FromJson()` and dictionary loading behavior for cleaner exception handling and path resolution consistency.\n            - Missing external JSON/CBOR dictionary files now surface proper `FileNotFoundException` errors for safer fallback handling.\n            - Corrupted JSON/CBOR payloads now expose their original exceptions directly for easier debugging and validation.\n            - Improved XML documentation across dictionary loading, customization, serialization, and normalization APIs.\n            - Hardened public API surface: `OfficeDocConverter.SupportedFormats` is read-only and `DictionaryLib.PlanCache` is no longer externally replaceable.\n            - Clarified async Office/EPUB conversion cancellation behavior and added pre-start cancellation checks.\n            - Existing GUI applications and core conversion behavior remain unchanged.",
